            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous rupture of left ventricular true aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1106-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The rupture of left ventricular true aneurysm is a rare event. We report the case of a 52-year-old man who presented to the emergency department with cardiac tamponade that was due to a ruptured left ventricular true aneurysm. An emergency operation was successfully performed to address this rare event.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
